# Build outputs, ignored for every workload below this directory.
#
# configs.json is emitted by main_bingo.py (--configs_out) as one of the three products of a
# single make rule, alongside the two generated headers; `make clean-data` deletes it. The
# per-workload .gitignore files already cover the headers with `*.h`, but nothing covered the
# JSON, so four of the thirty-seven workloads that emit one had it committed by accident.
#
# Tracking a generated file here is not cosmetic. A build rewrites it whenever params.hjson
# changes, so a sweep leaves the tree dirty and the committed copy silently disagrees with the
# params it was generated from; a `make clean-data` shows up as deleted tracked files.
configs.json
